    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers squarely on **Mickey Moniak**, who earns the day's highest rating at 75.98. His start against Ryan Gusto is primed for production, bolstered by a significant +14% park boost and favorable delivery metrics from the mound that elevate his stolen base probability. While **Josh Naylor** (67.18) serves as the anchor of our lineup, securing a strong rating despite a slight park penalty, the platoon advantage afforded to **Mickey Moniak** makes him the engine of our daily efficiency. We are also tracking **Alex Freeland** (55.18) and **Kyle Karros** (56.13); both benefit from the exploitable xERA of Randy V\u00e1squez and Ryan Gusto, respectively, keeping them safely above our marginal threshold despite lower-order batting assignments.\n\nThe bench decision process was heavily influenced by our prioritization of speed and efficiency, leading to the exclusion of **Cole Young** (45.04). While **Cole Young** technically cleared the floor threshold, he was ultimately bypassed due to the optimization of catcher-based defensive metrics that neutralized his potential value. Meanwhile, **Zach McKinstry** (36.89) and **Edwin Arroyo** (35.57) were benched as they fell below the 40.0 efficiency floor, the latter facing a brutal matchup against the elite arm of Misiorowski. We continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story**, who remains unavailable on the IL, while the uncertainty surrounding **Dalton Rushing**'s lineup placement remains a risk; should he be shifted further down the order, his utility score will be strictly monitored against our remaining reserves. **Austin Riley** (51.27) and **Brice Turang** (48.50) remain in the lineup as steady contributors, though their scores are tempered by tough matchups against Dustin May and Ch Burns.",
